#!/bin/sh
# First adoption: copy every existing destination this repo manages into a private backup
# before chezmoi changes anything (run_once_: runs again only if this script changes).
# tests/chezmoi.sh checks that this list covers everything `chezmoi managed` reports.
set -eu
dest={{ .chezmoi.destDir | shellQuote }}
backup="$dest/.local/state/pi-dotfiles/adoption-backup-$(date '+%Y%m%d%H%M%S')"
count=0
for rel in .pi/agent/AGENTS.md .pi/agent/settings.json .pi/agent/mcp.json .pi/agent/MEMORY.md .pi/agent/extensions .pi/agent/skills/prompt-engineering .claude/CLAUDE.md .codex/AGENTS.md .local/bin/prompt-opt .local/bin/prompt-opt-history.mjs ai/prompt_engineering; do
  if [ -e "$dest/$rel" ] || [ -L "$dest/$rel" ]; then
    mkdir -p "$(dirname "$backup")"
    [ -d "$backup" ] || mkdir -m 700 "$backup"
    mkdir -p "$backup/$(dirname "$rel")"
    cp -RP "$dest/$rel" "$backup/$rel"
    count=$((count + 1))
  fi
done
[ "$count" -eq 0 ] || echo "pi-dotfiles: backed up $count existing path(s) to $backup" >&2
